ity\": {\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/build.schema.json:39:      \"description\": \"Field names adapters/<name>/conformance.json declares this adapter can supply with a real value (vendor independence, 2026-09-09 ruling) -- [] when the adapter declares no conformance.json. Dollars are never summed across adapters; a field absent here renders as not reported by this executor, never zero or blank.\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/build.schema.json:107:      \"required\": [\"class\", \"provenance\", \"detail\"],\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/build.schema.json:111:          \"enum\": [\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/build.schema.json:112:                   \"ceiling\", \"claims-boundary\", \"repeated-act\", \"unclassed\", \"question\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/build.schema.json:115:        \"provenance\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"product\", \"tenant\", \"executor\", \"spec\"]},\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/build.schema.json:118:          \"description\": \"Populated for class \\\"unclassed\\\" (the log's last line, capped at 200 characters), class \\\"question\\\" (the halt's own question, its first line only), class \\\"environment\\\" ([checks].command's last output line, capped at 200 characters), and class \\\"gate\\\" (a refused spec-gate record's own refusal string, issue #137 -- never persisted on an actual build record; read here only because stop_class_enum sources the enum from this schema); null for every other class, whose evidence already lives in refusal, halted, or the log itself.\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:54:question: this adapter re-invokes the executor once, appending\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:376:        \"one class (the stop's class, or \\\"unclassed\\\"), one verdict -- \"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:411:        return (\"[executor.claude-code].allowed_tools is retired (issue \"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:430:    something [executor.claude-code] can set.\"\"\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:558:def question_class(status: str, question: str | None) -> str:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:663:def stream_line_events(obj: dict) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:735:            for kind, text in stream_line_events(obj):\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:784:    non-question costs two executor turns, and a report line built from\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:861:        # stays adapter-agnostic for tests/test_executor_conformance.py.\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:913:    cls = question_class(status, question)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:937:        cls2 = question_class(status2, question2)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:944:        # A non-question costs two executor turns, not one: sum both\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/run:960:                  \"-- the executor reported instead of asking, twice in \"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:25:      \"description\": \"Copied verbatim from [executor.<adapter>] merged with [executor.<adapter>.verify]; {} when no adapter was called.\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:32:      \"description\": \"Field names adapters/<name>/conformance.json declares this adapter can supply with a real value (vendor independence, 2026-09-09 ruling) -- [] when no adapter was called or it declares no conformance.json. Dollars are never summed across adapters; a field absent here renders as not reported by this executor, never zero or blank.\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:109:      \"required\": [\"class\", \"provenance\", \"detail\"],\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:113:          \"enum\": [\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:114:                   \"ceiling\", \"claims-boundary\", \"repeated-act\", \"unclassed\", \"question\"]\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:116:        \"provenance\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"product\", \"tenant\", \"executor\", \"spec\"]},\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:119:          \"description\": \"Populated for class \\\"unclassed\\\" (the log's last line, capped at 200 characters) and class \\\"question\\\" (the halt's own question, its first line only); null for every other class, whose evidence already lives in forge_checks or the log itself.\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/README.md:3:Runs `claude -p` against the spec. Configured through `[executor.claude-code]`\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/README.md:14:- `model` — omitted means the executor's default. When set, passed as `--model`, and trusted verbatim as the record's `model` rather than picked out of the tool's own usage report (issue #77).\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/README.md:17:- `allowed_tools` is retired (issue #78): a manifest that still declares `[executor.claude-code].allowed_tools` is refused by name rather than silently accepted or ignored. See below.\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/README.md:22:a failure back on the next iteration — the executor is not the runner of\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/README.md:42:tenant used to grow one denial at a time; `[executor.claude-code]` no\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/claude-code/README.md:44:executor that needs a package index is a tenant fact for a later\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/counsel.schema.json:31:      \"description\": \"Copied verbatim from [executor.<adapter>] merged with [executor.<adapter>.counsel].\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/counsel.schema.json:59:      \"enum\": [\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/counsel.schema.json:60:               \"ceiling\", \"claims-boundary\", \"repeated-act\", \"unclassed\", null],\n    def total_tokens(key: str) -> int:\n        entry = model_usage[key]\n        return ((entry.get(\"inputTokens\", 0) or 0)\n                + (entry.get(\"cacheReadInputTokens\", 0) or 0)\n                + (entry.get(\"cacheCreationInputTokens\", 0) or 0)\n                + (entry.get(\"outputTokens\", 0) or 0))\n\n    winner = max(model_usage, key=total_tokens)\n    return winner, model_usage[winner].get(\"canonicalModel\")\n\n\ndef adapter_version() -> str:\n    try:\n        out = subprocess.run([\"claude\", \"--version\"], capture_output=True,\n                             text=True, check=False)\n    except OSError:\n        return \"\"\n    return out.stdout.strip()\n\n\nMIN_QUESTION_CHARS = 40\n\nREINSTRUCTION = (\n    \"your last answer was a report, not a question; either continue to \"\n    \"done, or ask one question ending in a question mark that names the \"\n    \"spec line or guard you cannot resolve\")\n\n\ndef question_class(status: str, question: str | None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\"done\" (no halt at all), \"fail\" (a question too short or absent to\n    be worth a person's judgment -- MIN_QUESTION_CHARS, unchanged since\n    v0.15.0), \"report\" (long enough but carries no \"?\" -- issue #88's\n    class A, a status update in the question channel), or \"question\" (a\n    real question).\"\"\"\n    if status != \"question\":\n        return \"done\"\n    if not question or len(question) < MIN_QUESTION_CHARS:\n        return \"fail\"\n    if \"?\" not in question:\n        return \"report\"\n    return \"question\"\n\n\ndef subagent_refusal(response: dict) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"None if response carries no spawned background work; else the\n    refusal naming the counts (issue #88, class B). Checked on the\n    response itself, not the flag that was supposed to forbid it --\n    tenant zero's specimen spawned three with the tool absent from\n    --allowedTools entirely, so the flag alone is not the mechanism.\"\"\"\n    stats = response.get(\"subagent_stats\") or {}\n    spawned = stats.get(\"spawned\") or 0\n    if not spawned:\n        return None\n    killed = stats.get(\"killed\") or {}\n    killed_total = sum(v or 0 for v in killed.values())\n    return (\n        f\"adapters/claude-code/run: refused: subagent_stats.spawned={spawned} \"\n        f\"-- the {' or '.join(SUBAGENT_TOOLS)} tool spawned work that can \"\n        f\"outlive this invocation (completed={stats.get('completed', 0)}, \"\n        f\"killed={killed_total}, \"\n        f\"started_in_background={stats.get('started_in_background', 0)})\")\n    if refusal:\n        sys.stderr.write(refusal + \"\\n\")\n        return 1\n\n    structured = response.get(\"structured_output\") or {}\n\n    if verifying:\n        common = report_fields(response, config.get(\"model\"))\n        if common is None:\n            return 1\n        # .get(), not \"or []\": an absent findings key must reach\n        # cmd_verify as None, distinct from an explicit empty list --\n        # that distinction is the whole fix for issue #46.\n        line = {**common,\n               \"findings\": structured.get(\"findings\"),\n               \"tests_named\": structured.get(\"tests_named\")}\n        print(json.dumps(line))\n        return 0\n\n    if counseling:\n        common = report_fields(response, config.get(\"model\"))\n        if common is None:\n            return 1\n        line = {**common,\n               \"class\": structured.get(\"class\"),\n               \"verdict\": structured.get(\"verdict\"),\n               \"citations\": structured.get(\"citations\"),\n               \"proposal\": structured.get(\"proposal\")}\n        print(json.dumps(line))\n        return 0\n\n    status = structured.get(\"status\", \"done\")\n    question = structured.get(\"question\")\n    cls = question_class(status, question)\n\n    if cls == \"fail\":\n        return 1\n\n    if cls == \"report\":\n        # Issue #88, class A: a report in the question channel is\n        # re-instructed once, in this same invocation, before it ever\n        # reaches a person.\n        reinstruction = instruction + \"\\n\\n\" + REINSTRUCTION\n        cmd2 = build_command(reinstruction, config, schema, stage)\n        exit_code2, response2 = invoke_once(cmd2, responses, 1, events_path)\n        if exit_code2 is not None:\n            return exit_code2\n        if response2.get(\"is_error\") or not response2.get(\"structured_output\"):\n            return 1\n        refusal2 = subagent_refusal(response2)\n        if refusal2:\n            sys.stderr.write(refusal2 + \"\\n\")\n            return 1\n\n        structured2 = response2.get(\"structured_output\") or {}\n        status2 = structured2.get(\"status\", \"done\")\n        question2 = structured2.get(\"question\")\n        cls2 = question_class(status2, question2)\n        if cls2 == \"fail\":\n            return 1\n\n        common2 = report_fields(response2, config.get(\"model\"))\n        if common2 is None:\n            return 1\n        # A non-question costs two executor turns, not one: sum both\n        # calls' tokens and cost into the one report line this\n        # invocation gets, whatever the retry's own outcome -- only\n        # adapter_version/model/model_version stay the second call's.\n        tokens1_input, tokens1_output, cost1 = usage_fields(response)\n        common2[\"tokens\"][\"input\"] += tokens1_input\n        common2[\"tokens\"][\"output\"] += tokens1_output\n        common2[\"cost_usd\"] = add_cost(common2[\"cost_usd\"], cost1)\n\n        if cls2 == \"report\":\n            # Two reports in a row: still a halt (someone must look),\n            # but the transcript above already carries both raw\n            # results, and this report line names the class so a\n            # reader -- or a future record field, not this one -- can\n            # tell it apart from a genuine question.\n            print(\"adapters/claude-code/run: halted: class non-question \"\n                  \"-- the executor reported instead of asking, twice in \"\n                  \"a row\")\n            line = {**common2, \"status\": \"question\", \"question\": question2,\n                   \"class\": \"non-question\"}\n            print(json.dumps(line))\n            return 0\n\n        line = {**common2, \"status\": status2, \"question\": question2}\n        print(json.dumps(line))\n        return 0\n\n64:+tail -1 \"$tmp/out.txt\" | python3 -c 'import sys,json; l=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); assert l[\"status\"] == \"question\" and l[\"class\"] == \"non-question\", l; assert l[\"tokens\"][\"input\"] > 0, l'\n89:+grep -rq 'def test_claude_code_null_question_is_a_report_and_ends_as_non_question' tests/ && grep -rq 'def test_claude_code_ignores_a_stream_event_with_a_string_message' tests/\n98:+The claude-code adapter reads the executor's output as if its shapes were the adapter's to assume. Two failures on 2026-09-17, three and one specimens: an executor that ended its turn with `status: question, question: null` (a status update in the question channel, three times: #148 build-01, #151 build-01, #153 build-01) was classed `fail` by `question_class`, exit 1 with no report line, so each record is `no-cause / executor` with detail null, tokens 0, and ten minutes lost; and a stream line whose `message` was a string (#151 build-02) raised `AttributeError` inside `stream_line_events`, exit 1, `unclassed / product`, and 1064 s lost. `question_class` already has the class for the first (`report`, issue #88: a re-invocation with the nudge, then `non-question` with both results kept); the null question fell one branch short of it. The second is one field guarded of many.\n112:+- a-null-question-is-a-report.sh: a recorded stream whose result is status question with question null exits 0 with a report line of status question and class non-question carrying the tokens spent\n176:+its report line carries \"class\": \"non-question\" and both raw results\n677:+def question_class(status: str, question: str | None) -> str:\n721:+    #88: the non-question retry is a second invocation inside the same\n785:+def stream_line_events(obj: dict) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n866:+            for kind, text in stream_line_events(obj):\n915:+    non-question costs two executor turns, and a report line built from\n1044:+    cls = question_class(status, question)\n1068:+        cls2 = question_class(status2, question2)\n1075:+        # A non-question costs two executor turns, not one: sum both\n1090:+            print(\"adapters/claude-code/run: halted: class non-question \"\n1094:+                   \"class\": \"non-question\"}\n1174:+its report line carries \"class\": \"non-question\" and both raw results\n1675:+def question_class(status: str, question: str | None) -> str:\n1716:+    #88: the non-question retry is a second invocation inside the same\n1780:+def stream_line_events(obj: dict) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n1852:+            for kind, text in stream_line_events(obj):\n1901:+    non-question costs two executor turns, and a report line built from\n2030:+    cls = question_class(status, question)\n2054:+        cls2 = question_class(status2, question2)\n2061:+        # A non-question costs two executor turns, not one: sum both\n2076:+            print(\"adapters/claude-code/run: halted: class non-question \"\n2080:+                   \"class\": \"non-question\"}\n2113:+def test_claude_code_ignores_a_stream_event_with_a_string_message(tmp_path):\n2130:+def test_claude_code_null_question_is_a_report_and_ends_as_non_question(tmp_path):\n2131:+    null_question = dict(RESULT_LINE, structured_output={\"status\": \"question\", \"question\": None})\n2132:+    run = run_with_stream(tmp_path, [null_question])\n2136:+    assert line[\"class\"] == \"non-question\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '108,145p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '632,705p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '650,750p' adapters/claude-code/run; sed -n '640,820p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpysxho9f4/diff.patch; sed -n '2080,2150p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpysxho9f4/diff.patch; sed -n '1,180p' attest/specs/160/criteria/a-null-question-is-a-report.sh; sed -n '1,180p' attest/specs/160/criteria/a-string-message-is-transcript-not-a-crash.sh; sed -n '1,100p' attest/specs/160/criteria/the-boundary-has-its-tests.sh\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '108,145p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '632,705p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '650,750p' adapters/claude-code/run; sed -n '640,820p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpysxho9f4/diff.patch; sed -n '2080,2150p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpysxho9f4/diff.patch; sed -n '1,180p' attest/specs/160/criteria/a-null-question-is-a-report.sh; sed -n '1,180p' attest/specs/160/criteria/a-string-message-is-transcript-not-a-crash.sh; sed -n '1,100p' attest/specs/160/criteria/the-boundary-has-its-tests.sh\"","aggregated_output":"retires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\nfull rules both enforce.\n\nfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\nissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\nclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\nlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\nbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\nfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\nthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\ncommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\nnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\nempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\ncould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\n\ncounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\nwhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\npoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\napproval or executor spend (issue #133) -- and asks the tenant's\n[executor].counsel adapter (defaulting to [executor].verify) a\nread-only question about it: the record, its log, the spec (problem,\nclaims, criteria, stub, including stub/.removed), paths.rulings, the\nitem's diff since approval, the tenant manifest, and this product's own\nroot (bin/attavo, adapters/, schema/, templates/) by path, under the\nsame sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\nstop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\ncitations; patch: a product defect's file, symbol, rejection test, and\ndiff; person: a one-line question no rule covers), citations\n(instruction, mechanism, guard, each a path and symbol or a ruling id),\nand proposal (the ruling text, the patch, or the question). It writes\nthe next counsel-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with the adapter's\ntranscript beside it as counsel-NN.log, and commits nothing -- the\ncaller commits, as with every stage. It refuses (exit 1, nothing\nwritten) when the item carries no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate\nrecord to counsel. See issue #100's lane for the full rules it\nenforces, and issue #133's for the spec-gate fallback.\n\nrecord-only exits 0 when HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\n                refusal_provenance: str | None = None) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"The stop field for a build or verify record: None for status \"pass\",\n    else {class, provenance, detail} from what the caller already knows.\n\n      - report_class -- payload.get(\"class\") off the adapter's own report\n        line (issue #88, #94), when it names a STOP_CLASSES member -- is\n        that class, provenance \"executor\". build.schema.json and\n        verify.schema.json stay untouched by issue #88 on purpose, so the\n        class lives only on the report line, never a structured field\n        cmd_build or cmd_verify forwards on its own account; the caller\n        reads payload itself and passes this in, since only it still has\n        payload once an iteration ends. This is non-question's and\n        outlived-invocation's only path to a record now (issue #94):\n        CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS disables both for the text scan below, the\n        same way issue #93 disabled ceiling's bare-name match there. A\n        class an adapter does not yet put on its report line --\n        outlived-invocation today, since that refusal path prints no\n        report line at all -- falls to unclassed below, same as any\n        other unnamed cause, until the adapter that raises it puts a\n        class on the line the way non-question already does.\n      - a halt carrying a non-empty halted.question, once it is not a\n        non-question caught above, is a genuine question -- question/spec,\n        with the question's own first line as detail (issue #100's\n        followups). This is the specimen issue #100 itself was built to\n        retire: tenant zero's #663 build-01, a proper question, classed\n        unclassed/product and filed as a product defect with the wrong\n        provenance -- a question is about the definition of done, which is\n        a person's or a ruling's to answer, never the product's own\n        mechanism.\n      - failing that, a refusal or the log itself that already names its\n        class in text (issue #88, #93 for ceiling's own pre-emptive\n        refusal) is that class, provenance \"executor\" -- the log is\n        checked because neither adapter's refusal *field* carries the\n        class today; the class-naming line each adapter prints reaches\n        only the transcript\n      - a refusal that is not that -- the write-outside-claims path\n        itself, not the \"commit ... not authored by the executor\" shape\n        -- is claims-boundary/spec, unless the caller already knows this\n        refusal touched paths.records or paths.specs (issue #140:\n        protected_path_touched, checked ahead of the ordinary claims\n        match in cmd_build) and passes refusal_provenance=\"executor\" --\n        the product's own directories are not a claim a spec makes, so a\n        refusal there is not the spec's boundary to answer for\n      - a returned verify (the forge was not green; no adapter ran) is\n        forge-unconcluded/tenant\n      - an adapter exit whose log carries a declared-ceiling error line is\n        ceiling/product\n      - anything else is unclassed/product, with the log's last line\n        (capped at UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS) as its detail -- the other\n        class that carries a detail, since every remaining class's\n        evidence already lives in refusal, halted, forge_checks, or the\n        log itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if status == \"pass\":\n        return None\n    if status == \"returned\":\n        return {\"class\": \"forge-unconcluded\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": None}\n    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\n        return {\"class\": report_class, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n    question = (halted or {}).get(\"question\")\n    if status == \"halted\" and question:\n        return {\"class\": \"question\", \"provenance\": \"spec\",\n               \"detail\": question.splitlines()[0]}\n    known = _carries_a_known_class(refusal) or _carries_a_known_class(log)\n    if known:\n        return {\"class\": known, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n    if status == \"refused\" and refusal is not None and not refusal.startswith(\"commit \"):\n        return {\"class\": \"claims-boundary\", \"provenance\": refusal_provenance or \"spec\",\n               \"detail\": None}\n    if log and any(marker in log.lower() for marker in CEILING_MARKERS):\n        return {\"class\": \"ceiling\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": None}\n    return {\"class\": \"unclassed\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": _log_last_line(log)}\n\n\ndef tool_result_content_text(content) -> str:\n    \"\"\"A tool_result block's own text, whichever of claude code's two\n    content shapes it carries: a bare string, or a list of {\"type\":\n    \"text\", \"text\": ...} blocks (an image or other non-text block\n    contributes nothing -- there is no line of text to render).\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(content, str):\n        return content\n    if isinstance(content, list):\n        return \"\\n\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in content\n                         if isinstance(b, dict) and b.get(\"type\") == \"text\")\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef stream_line_events(obj: dict) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n    \"\"\"[(kind, text), ...] for one parsed stream-json line -- zero, one,\n    or several (one assistant turn can carry a text block and a tool_use\n    block together, each its own event). An assistant message's text\n    block maps to \"message\", its tool_use blocks to \"tool_call\" (the\n    tool's name and its first string argument); a user message carrying\n    a tool_result block maps to \"tool_result\" (the result's own first\n    line). Everything else on the stream -- system, and \"result\" itself,\n    read separately for the report fields rather than rendered as a feed\n    line -- maps to nothing.\"\"\"\n    events: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    content = ((obj.get(\"message\") or {}).get(\"content\") or [])\n    if obj.get(\"type\") == \"assistant\":\n        for block in content:\n            if not isinstance(block, dict):\n                continue\n            if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\" and block.get(\"text\"):\n                events.append((\"message\", block[\"text\"]))\n            elif block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n                name = block.get(\"name\") or \"\"\n                arg = first_string_arg(block.get(\"input\"))\n                events.append((\"tool_call\", f\"{name} {arg}\".strip()))\n    elif obj.get(\"type\") == \"user\":\n        for block in content:\n            if isinstance(block, dict) and block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_result\":\n                text = tool_result_content_text(block.get(\"content\"))\n                first_line = text.splitlines()[0] if text.splitlines() else \"\"\n                events.append((\"tool_result\", first_line))\n    return events\n\n\nEVENT_TEXT_MAX_CHARS = 400\n\n\ndef append_event(events_path: str, kind: str, text: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"One {at, kind, text} JSON line appended to events_path and\n    flushed at once -- the same shape and the same open-write-close\n    discipline bin/attavo's own append_event uses for its iteration and\n    gate events, kept independently here since an adapter is a separate\n    process with no import path into the product.\"\"\"\n    line = {\"at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\"),\n           \"kind\": kind, \"text\": \" \".join(text.split())[:EVENT_TEXT_MAX_CHARS]}\n    with open(events_path, \"a\") as fh:\n        fh.write(json.dumps(line) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef invoke_stream(cmd: list[str], events_path: str | None, canned_lines: list[str] | None\n                  ) -> tuple[str, dict | None, int]:\n    \"\"\"(raw transcript text, the terminal \"result\" object or None, exit\n    code) -- from canned_lines (ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE) when given,\n    else a real `claude --output-format stream-json --verbose`\n    invocation, read line by line as it runs (not buffered until the\n    process exits) so each mapped event reaches events_path while the\n    stage is still in progress. Every raw line reaches the returned\n    transcript, mapped or not -- issue #34's guarantee: the evidence is\n    what build-NN.log saves, not just what this adapter went on to use.\n    \"\"\"\n    raw_lines: list[str] = []\n    result: dict | None = None\n\n    def handle(line: str) -> None:\n        nonlocal result\n        if not line.strip():\n            return\n        raw_lines.append(line)\n        obj = parse_stream_line(line)\n        if obj is None:\n            return\n        if obj.get(\"type\") == \"result\":\n            result = obj\n            return\n        if events_path:\n            for kind, text in stream_line_events(obj):\n                append_event(events_path, kind, text)\n\n    if canned_lines is not None:\n        for line in canned_lines:\n            handle(line)\n        return \"\\n\".join(raw_lines), result, 0\n\n    proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)\n    assert proc.stdout is not None\n    for line in proc.stdout:\n        handle(line.rstrip(\"\\n\"))\n    proc.wait()\n    stderr = proc.stderr.read() if proc.stderr else \"\"\n    if stderr.strip():\n        raw_lines.append(stderr.rstrip(\"\\n\"))\n+        model_version = next(\n+            (key for key, entry in model_usage.items()\n+             if entry.get(\"canonicalModel\") == requested_model),\n+            None)\n+        return requested_model, model_version\n+\n+    if not model_usage:\n+        return None, None\n+\n+    def total_tokens(key: str) -> int:\n+        entry = model_usage[key]\n+        return ((entry.get(\"inputTokens\", 0) or 0)\n+                + (entry.get(\"cacheReadInputTokens\", 0) or 0)\n+                + (entry.get(\"cacheCreationInputTokens\", 0) or 0)\n+                + (entry.get(\"outputTokens\", 0) or 0))\n+\n+    winner = max(model_usage, key=total_tokens)\n+    return winner, model_usage[winner].get(\"canonicalModel\")\n+\n+\n+def adapter_version() -> str:\n+    try:\n+        out = subprocess.run([\"claude\", \"--version\"], capture_output=True,\n+                             text=True, check=False)\n+    except OSError:\n+        return \"\"\n+    return out.stdout.strip()\n+\n+\n+MIN_QUESTION_CHARS = 40\n+\n+REINSTRUCTION = (\n+    \"your last answer was a report, not a question; either continue to \"\n+    \"done, or ask one question ending in a question mark that names the \"\n+    \"spec line or guard you cannot resolve\")\n+\n+\n+def question_class(status: str, question: str | None) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"\"done\" (no halt at all), \"fail\" (a question too short or absent to\n+    be worth a person's judgment -- MIN_QUESTION_CHARS, unchanged since\n+    v0.15.0), \"report\" (long enough but carries no \"?\" -- issue #88's\n+    class A, a status update in the question channel), or \"question\" (a\n+    real question).\"\"\"\n+    if status != \"question\":\n+        return \"done\"\n+    if not question or len(question) < MIN_QUESTION_CHARS:\n+        # An absent or too-short question is a report with nothing in\n+        # it: a status update in the question channel (issue #150, three\n+        # specimens on 2026-09-17), never an exit with no report line.\n+        return \"report\"\n+    if \"?\" not in question:\n+        return \"report\"\n+    return \"question\"\n+\n+\n+def subagent_refusal(response: dict) -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"None if response carries no spawned background work; else the\n+    refusal naming the counts (issue #88, class B). Checked on the\n+    response itself, not the flag that was supposed to forbid it --\n+    tenant zero's specimen spawned three with the tool absent from\n+    --allowedTools entirely, so the flag alone is not the mechanism.\"\"\"\n+    stats = response.get(\"subagent_stats\") or {}\n+    spawned = stats.get(\"spawned\") or 0\n+    if not spawned:\n+        return None\n+    killed = stats.get(\"killed\") or {}\n+    killed_total = sum(v or 0 for v in killed.values())\n+    return (\n+        f\"adapters/claude-code/run: refused: subagent_stats.spawned={spawned} \"\n+        f\"-- the {' or '.join(SUBAGENT_TOOLS)} tool spawned work that can \"\n+        f\"outlive this invocation (completed={stats.get('completed', 0)}, \"\n+        f\"killed={killed_total}, \"\n+        f\"started_in_background={stats.get('started_in_background', 0)})\")\n+\n+\n+def load_canned_responses() -> list[dict] | None:\n+    \"\"\"None when ATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE is unset. Otherwise the\n+    queue this run answers from: a single object repeats for every\n+    invocation this adapter makes (unchanged since v0.3.0 -- most tests\n+    make exactly one), a JSON array is consumed in order, one response\n+    per invocation, its last element repeating once exhausted (issue\n+    #88: the non-question retry is a second invocation inside the same\n+    adapter run, and a canned test needs to hand it a different answer\n+    than the first). Distinct from ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE below: a\n+    canned response here is the final report object itself, the shape\n+    the model-derivation and report-field tests exercise, never a stream\n+    to map -- unaffected by --output-format actually being stream-json\n+    on a real invocation.\"\"\"\n+    response_file = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE\")\n+    if not response_file:\n+        return None\n+    raw = json.loads(Path(response_file).read_text())\n+    return raw if isinstance(raw, list) else [raw]\n+\n+\n+def load_canned_stream() -> list[str] | None:\n+    \"\"\"None when ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE is unset. Otherwise a\n+    recorded `claude --output-format stream-json --verbose` transcript,\n+    one JSONL line per list entry (issue #26, acceptance row 3) -- fed\n+    through the same line-by-line mapping and terminal \"result\" read a\n+    real invocation gets, so the mapping is exercised without a live\n+    `claude` process.\"\"\"\n+    stream_file = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE\")\n+    if not stream_file:\n+        return None\n+    return Path(stream_file).read_text().splitlines()\n+\n+\n+def parse_stream_line(line: str) -> dict | None:\n+    \"\"\"One parsed JSONL line, or None when it is blank or not JSON -- a\n+    tracing line on the same stream is not an error, just not an event\n+    (codex's own parse_events does the same).\"\"\"\n+    line = line.strip()\n+    if not line:\n+        return None\n+    try:\n+        return json.loads(line)\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return None\n+\n+\n+def first_string_arg(tool_input: dict | None) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"The first string-valued argument of a tool_use block's input, in\n+    declaration order -- a file path or a command, the one value worth a\n+    feed line; a tool whose arguments are all non-string (booleans,\n+    numbers) reports \"\" rather than guess which one matters.\"\"\"\n+    for value in (tool_input or {}).values():\n+        if isinstance(value, str):\n+            return value\n+    return \"\"\n+\n+\n+def tool_result_content_text(content) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"A tool_result block's own text, whichever of claude code's two\n+    content shapes it carries: a bare string, or a list of {\"type\":\n+    \"text\", \"text\": ...} blocks (an image or other non-text block\n+    contributes nothing -- there is no line of text to render).\"\"\"\n+    if isinstance(content, str):\n+        return content\n+    if isinstance(content, list):\n+        return \"\\n\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in content\n+                         if isinstance(b, dict) and b.get(\"type\") == \"text\")\n+    return \"\"\n+\n+\n+def stream_line_events(obj: dict) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n+    \"\"\"[(kind, text), ...] for one parsed stream-json line -- zero, one,\n+    or several (one assistant turn can carry a text block and a tool_use\n+    block together, each its own event). An assistant message's text\n+    block maps to \"message\", its tool_use blocks to \"tool_call\" (the\n+    tool's name and its first string argument); a user message carrying\n+    a tool_result block maps to \"tool_result\" (the result's own first\n+    line). Everything else on the stream -- system, and \"result\" itself,\n+    read separately for the report fields rather than rendered as a feed\n+    line -- maps to nothing.\"\"\"\n+    events: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n+    # The stream is the executor's; its shapes are not the adapter's to\n+    # assume. A line whose message is not an object (a diagnostic with a\n+    # string message, attavo/attavo#151 build-02) maps to nothing and\n+    # stays transcript; nothing here raises on a shape it did not expect.\n+    message = obj.get(\"message\")\n+    if not isinstance(message, dict):\n+        return events\n+    content = message.get(\"content\") or []\n+    if not isinstance(content, list):\n+        return events\n+    if obj.get(\"type\") == \"assistant\":\n+        for block in content:\n+            if not isinstance(block, dict):\n+                continue\n+            if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\" and block.get(\"text\"):\n+                events.append((\"message\", block[\"text\"]))\n+            elif block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n+                name = block.get(\"name\") or \"\"\n+                arg = first_string_arg(block.get(\"input\"))\n+                events.append((\"tool_call\", f\"{name} {arg}\".strip()))\n+    elif obj.get(\"type\") == \"user\":\n+        for block in content:\n+            if isinstance(block, dict) and block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_result\":\n+                text = tool_result_content_text(block.get(\"content\"))\n+                first_line = text.splitlines()[0] if text.splitlines() else \"\"\n+                   \"class\": \"non-question\"}\n+            print(json.dumps(line))\n+            return 0\n+\n+        line = {**common2, \"status\": status2, \"question\": question2}\n+        print(json.dumps(line))\n+        return 0\n+\n+    common = report_fields(response, config.get(\"model\"))\n+    if common is None:\n+        return 1\n+    line = {**common, \"status\": status, \"question\": question}\n+    print(json.dumps(line))\n+    return 0\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    sys.exit(main())\ndiff --git a/attest/specs/160/stub/tests/test_adapter_boundary.py b/attest/specs/160/stub/tests/test_adapter_boundary.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f267078\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/specs/160/stub/tests/test_adapter_boundary.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+\"\"\"adapters/claude-code/run at its boundary with the executor's output:\n+nothing on the stream makes the adapter raise, and an absent question is\n+a report, never an exit with no report line (attavo/attavo#150 and the\n+#151 build-02 crash, 2026-09-17).\"\"\"\n+import json\n+\n+from test_adapter_claude_code import RESULT_LINE, read_events, run_with_stream\n+\n+\n+def test_claude_code_ignores_a_stream_event_with_a_string_message(tmp_path):\n+    diagnostic = {\"type\": \"rate_limit_event\", \"message\": \"rate limit status\"}\n+    run = run_with_stream(tmp_path, [diagnostic, RESULT_LINE])\n+    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n+    assert json.dumps(diagnostic) in run.stdout\n+    assert json.loads(run.stdout.splitlines()[-1])[\"status\"] == \"done\"\n+    assert read_events(tmp_path) == []\n+\n+\n+def test_claude_code_ignores_a_stream_event_whose_content_is_not_a_list(tmp_path):\n+    odd = {\"type\": \"assistant\", \"message\": {\"content\": \"a bare string\"}}\n+    run = run_with_stream(tmp_path, [odd, RESULT_LINE])\n+    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n+    assert json.loads(run.stdout.splitlines()[-1])[\"status\"] == \"done\"\n+    assert read_events(tmp_path) == []\n+\n+\n+def test_claude_code_null_question_is_a_report_and_ends_as_non_question(tmp_path):\n+    null_question = dict(RESULT_LINE, structured_output={\"status\": \"question\", \"question\": None})\n+    run = run_with_stream(tmp_path, [null_question])\n+    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n+    line = json.loads(run.stdout.splitlines()[-1])\n+    assert line[\"status\"] == \"question\"\n+    assert line[\"class\"] == \"non-question\"\n+    assert line[\"tokens\"][\"input\"] > 0\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nhere=$(pwd)\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\": \"result\", \"is_error\": false, \"structured_output\": {\"status\": \"question\", \"question\": null}, \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 5, \"output_tokens\": 9}, \"total_cost_usd\": 0.01, \"modelUsage\": {\"claude-sonnet-5\": {\"inputTokens\": 5, \"outputTokens\": 9}}}' > \"$tmp/stream.jsonl\"\nenv -u ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR=\"$here/tests/fixtures/build_valid/specs/1\" ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR=\"$tmp/records\" ATTAVO_RULINGS=\"$tmp/rulings.md\" ATTAVO_BRANCH=attavo/1-example ATTAVO_ITERATION=1 ATTAVO_FEEDBACK=\"$tmp/feedback.txt\" ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE=\"$tmp/stream.jsonl\" python3 adapters/claude-code/run > \"$tmp/out.txt\" 2> \"$tmp/err.txt\"\ntail -1 \"$tmp/out.txt\" | python3 -c 'import sys,json; l=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); assert l[\"status\"] == \"question\" and l[\"class\"] == \"non-question\", l; assert l[\"tokens\"][\"input\"] > 0, l'\nrm -rf \"$tmp\"\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nhere=$(pwd)\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\": \"rate_limit_event\", \"message\": \"rate limit status\"}' '{\"type\": \"result\", \"is_error\": false, \"structured_output\": {\"status\": \"done\", \"question\": null}, \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 5, \"output_tokens\": 9}, \"total_cost_usd\": 0.01, \"modelUsage\": {\"claude-sonnet-5\": {\"inputTokens\": 5, \"outputTokens\": 9}}}' > \"$tmp/stream.jsonl\"\nenv -u ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR=\"$here/tests/fixtures/build_valid/specs/1\" ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR=\"$tmp/records\" ATTAVO_RULINGS=\"$tmp/rulings.md\" ATTAVO_BRANCH=attavo/1-example ATTAVO_ITERATION=1 ATTAVO_FEEDBACK=\"$tmp/feedback.txt\" ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE=\"$tmp/stream.jsonl\" ATTAVO_EVENTS=\"$tmp/events.jsonl\" python3 adapters/claude-code/run > \"$tmp/out.txt\" 2> \"$tmp/err.txt\"\ntail -1 \"$tmp/out.txt\" | python3 -c 'import sys,json; l=json.loads(sys.stdin.read()); assert l[\"status\"] == \"done\", l'\ngrep -q '\"rate limit status\"' \"$tmp/out.txt\"\ntest ! -s \"$tmp/events.jsonl\"\nrm -rf \"$tmp\"\n#!/bin/sh\ngrep -rq 'def test_claude_code_null_question_is_a_report_and_ends_as_non_question' tests/ && grep -rq 'def test_claude_code_ignores_a_stream_event_with_a_string_message' tests/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
